-2. **Reel label across two dates.** The retained October 8, 2003 ZOB-278 custody form carries a handwritten **4B 1344–1650** reading. Preserve it beside AGL-65's September 2001 label. This is a repeated reel-and-time description across two forms. An item identifier, transfer and return sequence and position-to-track register would test physical continuity and relation to later re-recordings. [ZOB-278](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/7597400)
-3. **The September 25 email time.** UAL93 item **2** prints **9/25/01 @12:26pm**, consistent with the earlier read of ZOB-244 and the nested email in ZOB-261. ZOB-261's enclosing reply still displays **12:02 PM**. The inventory is a separate description of a candidate message. It supplies neither an independent clock nor proof of website upload. Preserve the original displayed headers, their absence of clock validation, and the separate later reply. [Earlier Cleveland comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/5486d2e73b4e53e922946b41d3ac8b4b53cb20db/investigation/broader-evidence/faa-cleveland-request-returns-2026-11-05/README.md)
